;; the guest runs). Why this is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 6 (section 17): POC.EXE on the guest failed with an
;;   access violation compiling a type-bound call, in
;;   VaxCodeGenerator.MethodCallTarget: m.fromParam := ~m.fromBlock &
;;   (real = NIL) & (ParamTag(obj) # NIL). m's address was in R0, pinned
;;   as the field's base; the call on the right side's path moved it to R3
;;   (FreeR0R1) on that path only, and the store after the join, MOVB R2,
;;   25(R3), went through a stale R3 when m.fromBlock decided, overwriting
;;   the local method.
;; - Now ShortCircuit moves every pinned register out of R0 and R1 before
;;   its left side, as SpillAll already moved the others to the frame: in
;;   Set, MOVL R0, R2 comes before each branch, and both stores, MOVB R1,
;;   2(R2) and MOVB R1, 3(R2), go through R2 on either path.
;; - The result of the left side, R1, which the call does move (to R3),
;;   comes back to R1 before the join, as it did before (MOVB R3, R1).
;; - ShortOut, run on the guest under -O2 and -OC, prints what the LLVM
;;   build prints (output.expected): each case's flags and calls, both
;;   paths of each & and OR.
